6.Responsibilities of the CATPP and Cheyenne MPO
a.The CATPP and Cheyenne MPO's Unified Planning Work Programs(UPWPs) shall
be based on this funding allocation. Draft UPWPs will be submitted no later than
fifteen(15) days before the end ofthefiscal year.
b. One (1) copy of all draft products and two (2) copies of allfinal products and
documents generated from planning studies accomplished utilizing thesefunds shall be
forwarded toWYDOT for their review and files; and one (1) copy of all draft and one
(1) copy of all final products and documents generated from planning studies
accomplished utilizing these funds shall be forwarded toFHWA for their review and
files.
c.CATPP and the Cheyenne MPO will provide both annual and quarterly reports of
metropolitan planning activities to WYDOT.WYDOT shall make available similar
reporting to the MPOs of statewide planning activities utilizing PLfunds.
d. CATPP and the Cheyenne MPO shall adhere to all applicable Code of Federal
Regulation requirements involving metropolitan planning.
for all city and county business activities not directly related to the function of the
MPO.Such activities shall be considered non-re im burs able.
f.In the event that CATPP or Cheyenne MPO has a justifiable need for additional funds,
a written request shall be made toWYDOT specifying the work item(s)proposed for
use of the additional funds.
g. CATPP and the Cheyenne MPO shall adhere to all applicable provisions of their
current Master Agreement with WY DOT.
7.General Provisions,
a. Amendments. Either party may request changes to this MOU. Any changes,
modifications, revisions or amendments to this MOU which are mutually agreed upon
by and between the parties to this MOU shall be incorporated by written instrument,
executed and signed by all parties to this MOU.
b.Applicable Law and Venue.The construction, interpretation and enforcement of
this MOU shall be governed by the laws of the State of Wyoming.The courts of the
State of Wyoming shall have jurisdiction over any action arising out of thisMOU and
over the parties, and the venue shall be the First Judicial District, Laramie County,
Wyoming.
